      "reasoning": "Verified in the actual file. Lines 66-69 are exactly compileOnly(libs.android.gradlePlugin) and compileOnly(libs.kotlin.gradlePlugin). The [libraries] block (lines 26-45) defines only compose/koin/ktor/testing entries — there is no android-gradlePlugin or kotlin-gradlePlugin entry. Version-catalog accessors are generated solely from TOML entries, so both accessors are unresolved and build-logic/convention/build.gradle.kts will not compile. Compounding this, the file shows no build-logic/settings.gradle.kts and the root settings.gradle.kts (lines 114-129) never calls includeBuild(\"build-logic\"), so the 'libs' catalog is not visible inside the composite build anyway. rcosteira's android-gradle-logic lines 14-23 and checklist line 53 document exactly this gotcha. Both parts of the claim are accurate; this is a real defect in the centerpiece example."
    },
    {
      "description": "ahmed gradle-patterns: feature module applies plugin ids convention.android.library and convention.android.compose, but no convention plugin is registered under those ids and no compose convention plugin class exists (minor).",
      "verdict": "CONFIRMED",
      "reasoning": "Verified. Lines 135-138 apply id(\"convention.android.library\") and id(\"convention.android.compose\"). The only convention plugin class shown is AndroidLibraryConventionPlugin (lines 72-89), with no gradlePlugin { plugins { register(...) } } block declaring an id, and no compose convention plugin defined anywhere. Applying an id that is never registered fails configuration with 'Plugin [id: ...] was not found'. rcosteira's checklist line 54 flags that convention plugins must be register-ed with stable ids. Technically accurate; minor is appropriate since it is illustrative documentation code."
